WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.402
-My next guest is
a very talented actress

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:06.005
starring on the hit
television series "Bridgerton."

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:08.474
Season 1 is
streaming now on Netflix.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:10.677
Here's Phoebe Dynevor,
everybody!

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.777
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:14.247
-Oh, my goodness! Hello!

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.115
Phoebe Dynevor!
-Hi!

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:19.218
-Hello and welcome.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:20.653
Thank you for coming on.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.155
It's your first time
on our show.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:26.226
-Yes. I'm so happy to be here.
Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:29.762
-I want to --
-I'm your biggest fan.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.297
-Alright,
well, right back at you.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:32.565
Alright, here we go.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.734
I do -- I want to
talk to you about "Bridgerton,"

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.803
but I also want to say we
just had Lin-Manuel Miranda

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:39.038
out here on the show,

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:41.007
and I know that
you're a big fan of Lin and...

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.842
-[ Breathes deeply ]

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.345
Can we just talk about
"Hamilton" this whole interview?

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.980
Because I'm the biggest fan
of Lin-Manuel ever.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.181
-Wait, wait. Hold on a second.

00:00:49.181 --> 00:00:52.452
But, you know,
there's Lin, who was here,

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.687
but then there's me,
who is here, you know?

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:58.124
-Yeah, both of you
in the same room is crazy.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.693
I don't know what
to do with myself right now.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.162
But Lin-Manuel --
"Hamilton" literally got me

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:04.731
and my family through lockdown.

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:07.733
We would play it
every single day.

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:11.304
We watched the theater version
a million times

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.840
and we can sing every song.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.409
So, yeah, "Hamilton"
is the best, the best.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.844
I cannot wait to see
"In the Heights."

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:20.479
-Oh, get ready.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:21.848
Get ready.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:22.982
-No, you won't even believe --

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.550
This Thursday,
you won't even believe it.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.687
Get ready. It pays off.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:30.389
But people will say the same
thing for you, by the way,

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:32.525
because you got us
through quarantine.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.694
We all got to experience
you with "Bridgerton"

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.429
and we all --
That was a moment.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.666
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's a TV moment.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:43.803
And that's amazing.
And it came out of nowhere.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.571
I had no idea.

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:47.273
We were just looking
for something to watch,

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.908
and everyone was like, "I'm in.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.810
It's 'Downton Abbey'
but spicier."

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.212
I don't know what it was,
but we didn't know what it was.

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:54.781
And it was so great.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.417
And I always love a good story,
as anyone does,

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.787
but the story of you getting
cast is interesting to me,

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.655
because I heard that you were
almost ready to just kind of

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.891
give up on acting in L.A.
for a little bit,

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.559
and you go,
"Eh, it's not working out.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:07.560
I'm going to go back
to England."

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.962
Is that true?

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.264
-Yeah. I had been --
It was kind of crazy.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.332
I've been living in L.A.
for about nine months

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:16.769
and I was kind of at that point
where I was ready to go home,

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:20.940
sort of throw in the towel,
and see the fam for a bit.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.809
And then I got a call saying,

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.478
"Can you come in and read with
Regé next week?"

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.913
And I was like "Oh, God.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:31.251
Well, that's annoying, 'cause
I've got to move my flight."

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.152
So I was like,
"I hope it pays off."

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:35.120
-Yeah. "I don't want to do this
and get rejected."

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:38.358
Yeah, exactly.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:40.859
And then --
Yeah, and then, the next day,

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:43.195
they were like,
"Netflix will pay

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:44.630
for your flight back to London,

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.799
because you've got to be in
rehearsals on Monday."

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:47.901
-That's what I'm talking about!
-So it did pay off.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:51.570
-Yes! That's the story
that you want.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.039
I love that!
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:54.039 --> 00:03:01.214
-When did you recognize that
you and Regé-Jean had chemistry?

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.148
Because Regé-Jean
has been on our show,

00:03:03.148 --> 00:03:05.751
and I had chemistry with
Regé-Jean.

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:07.554
-Yeah, it's hard not to.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:12.325
-Yeah, but you two together,
it's like, "What is going on?"

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.492
When did you guys realize it?

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:14.928
Was it rehearsal or was it --

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.296
Did you do a scene and you go,
"That's pretty good, guys."

00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:20.166
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.434
-I think you never know,

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.303
but we both had
dance rehearsals together

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:28.040
and we were both kind of nervous
about the dancing part.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.309
It was the part that
we were both a bit like,

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.244
"Oh, can we do this?"

00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:34.546
And I remember
we had a few rehearsals,

00:03:34.546 --> 00:03:39.719
and one of them got recorded so
we got to watch it back.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.653
And we were like,
"Oh, eye contact

00:03:41.653 --> 00:03:44.590
really does a lot of the work."

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:47.459
-Yeah, yeah. Yeah, you felt --
-And dancing.

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:48.961
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:52.564
Well, I think it was
brilliantly done.

00:03:52.564 --> 00:03:56.001
And we know that he's not
returning for Season 2, but --

00:03:56.001 --> 00:03:57.237
A lot of people
were disappointed,

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:59.071
but if you read
the books, which --

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:01.006
or read the books,
which I have not --

00:04:01.006 --> 00:04:03.042
So I was going, "Aww!"

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:06.812
And then they go, "No, that's
the way the story goes."

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:09.082
It was never planned for him
to return in Season 2.

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.583
Is that correct?

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.852
-No, I mean, I think every --

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.487
The special thing about
"Bridgerton"

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.956
that I think not a lot of
shows really do

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:21.060
is that every season centers
around a different love story.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:26.065
So, Season 2 is centered around
Anthony, my older brother,

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:28.233
and his sort of coming out
into the season

00:04:28.233 --> 00:04:30.802
and finding a match, hopefully.

00:04:30.802 --> 00:04:34.506
So, every story centers
around a different relationship.

00:04:34.506 --> 00:04:38.010
So, I'm just really excited
to watch the show as an audience

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.013
and see what it has
in store for him.

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:44.383
-But you're back and you're
filming Season 2 right now?

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:47.119
-Yeah, yeah.
I've had three days on set.

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:49.688
It's so nice to be back.

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:51.691
-What does it feel like?
-It's such a nice feeling.

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:53.325
Oh, it's the best.

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:58.631
I cried like seven times
when I came back,

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:02.435
'cause so much had happened, you
know, since the first season.

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:04.803
Obviously, COVID
and the show coming out

00:05:04.803 --> 00:05:06.638
and just seeing everyone again.

00:05:06.638 --> 00:05:09.375
I mean, half of their faces,
for the most part.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:12.144
But, yeah, it's just so nice.
-Still, I'll take it, yeah.

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:16.049
Well, on behalf of everyone
who actually did

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:17.650
get through quarantine
thanks to you,

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.151
I just want to say
thank you very much

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.419
for doing what you did.

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.855
It was definitely
a big moment for us.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.823
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:27.660
And I want to show everyone
a clip from Season 1.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:31.931
Here's Phoebe Dynevor and
Regé-Jean Page in "Bridgerton."

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:33.032
Take a look.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.433
-It would be better
if you refrained

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:36.168
from thinking about me at all.

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:38.971
-It is simply surprising.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.207
-Yes, how ever
is it possible for a lady

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:44.210
to offer anything but a smile
whilst seated beside a duke?

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.712
-You regarding subjects
much too...

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:48.381
-Even one of your reputation.
-You are aware of my reputation.

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:52.552
-I'm aware of your friendship
with my eldest brother.

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:54.653
If that were not enough,
I'm also aware of the things

00:05:54.653 --> 00:05:57.189
a certain writer
has recently written of you.

00:05:57.189 --> 00:05:58.357
Presumptuous?

00:05:58.357 --> 00:05:59.558
Clearly.

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:01.226
Arrogant? Most definitely.

00:06:01.226 --> 00:06:04.230
You are a rake
through and through.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.531
Tell me I'm wrong.

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.933
-Who is to refrain
from thinking about whom again?

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:10.769
-I assure you, I'm anything
but interested in you.

00:06:10.769 --> 00:06:11.871
-Good.
-Quite.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:14.206
-And I anything
but interested in you.

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:16.775
-There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.775 --> 00:06:18.611
Phoebe Dynevor, everybody!

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:22.215
Season 1 of "Bridgerton"
is streaming now on Netflix.

